    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "pieges",
     "title": "Common mistakes",
     "md": "- Forgetting to multiply by the scale (reading 4.5 cm as 4.5 km).\n- Measuring along the wrong line: use a ruler for straight distances.\n- Mixing the Equator (east-west line) and the Prime Meridian (north-south line).\n- Writing grid references with the wrong order: letter first, then number."
    },
